   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Reel\n\nA fixed centered card where images stack on the z-axis and each blooms open over the last. Five CSS-drawn placeholder screens stand in for your shots: a host swaps its own images in by replacing the contents of each .rl-shot with an img (object-fit cover).\n\nCategory: ui-blocks. Length: 5.333 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- Showing a sequence of screenshots or product shots that should bloom open one over the last in a fixed frame.\n- You want the reveal itself (the centre-out mask) to be the only motion in the scene.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You need a single framed photo rather than a sequence: use instant-photo.\n- You want a scrolling wall of items rather than a stacked reveal: use infinite-marquee or perspective-marquee.\n\nVariables:\n- width (number, 600-1280): Card width, default 1180\n- height (number, 360-720): Card height, default 676\n- radius (number, 0-40): Radius, default 16\n- step (number, 6-40): Frames per image, default 20\n- reveal (number, 4-30): Reveal frames, default 13\n- background_color (color): Card background, default \"#050506\"\n- stage_color (color): Stage, default \"#0b0b0c\"\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Reel\n\n  A fixed centered card where images stack on the z-axis and each blooms open over the last. Five CSS-drawn placeholder screens stand in for your shots: a host swaps its own images in by replacing the contents of each .rl-shot with an img (object-fit cover).\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/reel/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"reel\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"5.333\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"width\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Card width\", \"description\": \"Card width in px.\", \"default\": 1180, \"min\": 600, \"max\": 1280, \"step\": 20, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"height\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Card height\", \"description\": \"Card height in px.\", \"default\": 676, \"min\": 360, \"max\": 720, \"step\": 4, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"radius\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Radius\", \"description\": \"Corner radius.\", \"default\": 16, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 40, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"step\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Frames per image\", \"description\": \"Frames between one image starting and the next.\", \"default\": 20, \"min\": 6, \"max\": 40, \"step\": 1},\n    {\"id\": \"reveal\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Reveal frames\", \"description\": \"Frames for one image to open.\", \"default\": 13, \"min\": 4, \"max\": 30, \"step\": 1},\n    {\"id\": \"background_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Card background\", \"description\": \"Color behind the images.\", \"default\": \"#050506\"},\n    {\"id\": \"stage_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Stage\", \"description\": \"Frame background.\", \"default\": \"#0b0b0c\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Reel</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;600&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n\n        #root { background: var(--bg); }\n        .rl-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .rl-frame { position: relative; flex-shrink: 0; }\n        .rl-card { position: absolute; inset: 0; box-shadow: 0 30px 80px rgba(0,0,0,0.6); overflow: hidden; opacity: 0; }\n        .rl-shot { position: absolute; inset: 0; transform-origin: 50% 0%; font-family: Inter, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif; }\n        .rl-edge { position: absolute; inset: 0; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); }\n        /* Placeholder screens drawn in CSS. A host replaces the contents of .rl-shot with an img (object-fit: cover). */\n        .rl-bar { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 0; height: 9%; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.2%; padding: 0 2.5%; }\n        .rl-bar i { width: 1.1%; aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 50%; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.35); }\n        .rl-side { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 9%; bottom: 0; width: 17%; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.22); }\n        .rl-side b { display: block; height: 3.2%; margin: 12% 14% 0; border-radius: 99px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.18); }\n        .rl-tile { position: absolute; border-radius: 1.6%; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"reel\" data-duration=\"5.333\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"rl-clip\" class=\"rl-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"5.333\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div class=\"rl-frame\" id=\"rl-frame\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var NAME = \"reel\";\n\nvar root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\nvar vars = window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables() : {};\nfunction num(v, f, min, max) { var n = Number(v); return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : f; }\nfunction str(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v.trim() ? v : f; }\nfunction col(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && /^#([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6})$/i.test(v.trim()) ? v.trim() : f; }\nfunction bool(v, f) { return v === true || v === \"true\" ? true : v === false || v === \"false\" ? false : f; }\nvar FPS = 30;\nvar DUR = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"2\");\nvar TOTAL = Math.round(DUR * FPS);\nfunction lerp(a, b, t) { return a + (b - a) * t; }\nfunction cl(x, a, b) { return Math.min(b, Math.max(a, x)); }\n// interpolate(x, [in...], [out...], easing): clamped on both sides, easing applied per segment.\nfunction interp(x, inp, out, easing) {\n  if (x <= inp[0]) return out[0];\n  if (x >= inp[inp.length - 1]) return out[out.length - 1];\n  var i = 0;\n  while (x > inp[i + 1]) i++;\n  var t = (x - inp[i]) / (inp[i + 1] - inp[i]);\n  if (easing) t = easing(t);\n  return out[i] + (out[i + 1] - out[i]) * t;\n}\nfunction bez(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n  return function (x) {\n    if (x <= 0) return 0; if (x >= 1) return 1;\n    var t = x;\n    for (var i = 0; i < 8; i++) {\n      var cx = 3 * x1 * t * (1 - t) * (1 - t) + 3 * x2 * t * t * (1 - t) + t * t * t - x;\n      var d = 3 * x1 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) - 6 * x1 * t * (1 - t) + 6 * x2 * t * (1 - t) - 3 * x2 * t * t + 3 * t * t;\n      if (Math.abs(cx) < 1e-6 || Math.abs(d) < 1e-6) break;\n      t -= cx / d;\n    }\n    t = cl(t, 0, 1);\n    return 3 * y1 * t * (1 - t) * (1 - t) + 3 * y2 * t * t * (1 - t) + t * t * t;\n  };\n}\nvar E = {\n  lin: function (t) { return t; },\n  quad: function (t) { return t * t; },\n  cubic: function (t) { return t * t * t; },\n  sin: function (t) { return 1 - Math.cos((t * Math.PI) / 2); }\n};\nfunction eOut(f) { return function (t) { return 1 - f(1 - t); }; }\nfunction eInOut(f) { return function (t) { return t < 0.5 ? f(2 * t) / 2 : 1 - f(2 - 2 * t) / 2; }; }\nvar outCubic = eOut(E.cubic), outQuad = eOut(E.quad), inCubic = E.cubic, inQuad = E.quad;\nvar inOutCubic = eInOut(E.cubic), inOutQuad = eInOut(E.quad), inOutSin = eInOut(E.sin), outSin = eOut(E.sin);\n// Damped spring from 0 to 1 (rest at 1, no initial velocity), frames at 30 fps.\nfunction spring(frame, cfg) {\n  if (frame <= 0) return 0;\n  var m = cfg.mass || 1, k = cfg.stiffness, c = cfg.damping;\n  var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / m), z = c / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * m)), t = frame / FPS;\n  if (z < 1) {\n    var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n    return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + ((z * w0) / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n  }\n  if (z === 1) return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n  var s = w0 * Math.sqrt(z * z - 1), r1 = -z * w0 + s, r2 = -z * w0 - s;\n  return 1 - (r2 * Math.exp(r1 * t) - r1 * Math.exp(r2 * t)) / (r2 - r1);\n}\n// Seeded random: same string in, same number out.\nfunction rnd(seed) {\n  var sd = String(seed), h = 1779033703 ^ sd.length;\n  for (var i = 0; i < sd.length; i++) { h = Math.imul(h ^ sd.charCodeAt(i), 3432918353); h = (h << 13) | (h >>> 19); }\n  h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 16), 2246822507); h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 3266489909); h ^= h >>> 16;\n  var a = (h >>> 0);\n  a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a);\n  t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;\n  return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n}\nfunction rgb(h) {\n  h = h.replace(\"#\", \"\");\n  if (h.length === 3) h = h[0] + h[0] + h[1] + h[1] + h[2] + h[2];\n  return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16), parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16), parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16)];\n}\nfunction mixc(a, b, t) {\n  var x = rgb(a), y = rgb(b);\n  return \"rgb(\" + Math.round(lerp(x[0], y[0], t)) + \",\" + Math.round(lerp(x[1], y[1], t)) + \",\" + Math.round(lerp(x[2], y[2], t)) + \")\";\n}\nfunction rgba(h, a) { var x = rgb(h); return \"rgba(\" + x[0] + \",\" + x[1] + \",\" + x[2] + \",\" + a + \")\"; }\nvar SVGNS = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\nfunction svgEl(tag, attrs, parent) {\n  var e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);\n  for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);\n  if (parent) parent.appendChild(e);\n  return e;\n}\nfunction setA(e, attrs) { for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]); }\n// Drive draw(frame) from the timeline; frames run 0..frames over frames/30 seconds.\nfunction drive(draw, frames) {\n  var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n  var clock = { frame: 0 };\n  tl.to(clock, { frame: frames, duration: frames / FPS, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.frame); } }, 0);\n  draw(0);\n  return tl;\n}\nfunction finish(tl) {\n  if (tl.duration() < DUR) tl.to({}, { duration: DUR - tl.duration() });\n  tl.seek(0);\n  window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n  window.__timelines[NAME] = tl;\n}\n\n\nvar frameEl = document.getElementById(\"rl-frame\");\nvar cw = num(vars.width, 1180, 300, 1600), ch = num(vars.height, 676, 200, 900), radius = num(vars.radius, 16, 0, 60), stepF = num(vars.step, 20, 6, 40), revealF = num(vars.reveal, 13, 4, 30);\nvar bg = col(vars.background_color, \"#050506\"), stageBg = col(vars.stage_color, \"#0b0b0c\");\nroot.style.setProperty(\"--bg\", stageBg);\nvar W = root.clientWidth, H = root.clientHeight;\n// Cards are laid out at 1180 by 676 and scaled down when the frame is narrower than the card.\nvar scale = Math.min(1, (W * 0.94) / cw, (H * 0.9) / ch);\nframeEl.style.width = cw + \"px\"; frameEl.style.height = ch + \"px\"; frameEl.style.transform = \"scale(\" + scale + \")\";\nvar HUES = [[\"#3159ff\", \"#7c9bff\"], [\"#e5322d\", \"#ff8a7a\"], [\"#12a37f\", \"#7de3c3\"], [\"#a800b7\", \"#e08cff\"], [\"#f2a900\", \"#ffd96b\"]];\nfunction screen(h) {\n  var a = h[0], b = h[1];\n  return '<div class=\"rl-bar\"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class=\"rl-side\"><b></b><b></b><b></b><b></b></div>' +\n    '<div class=\"rl-tile\" style=\"left:21%;top:15%;width:34%;height:26%;background:linear-gradient(135deg,' + a + ',' + b + ')\"></div>' +\n    '<div class=\"rl-tile\" style=\"left:58%;top:15%;width:18%;height:26%;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.10)\"></div>' +\n    '<div class=\"rl-tile\" style=\"left:79%;top:15%;width:17%;height:26%;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.10)\"></div>' +\n    '<div class=\"rl-tile\" style=\"left:21%;top:46%;width:75%;height:46%;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.06)\"></div>' +\n    [0.3, 0.55, 0.4, 0.8, 0.65, 0.9, 0.5].map(function (v, i) { return '<div class=\"rl-tile\" style=\"left:' + (25 + i * 9.6) + '%;bottom:11%;width:5.4%;height:' + v * 34 + '%;background:' + (i % 2 ? b : a) + ';opacity:.85\"></div>'; }).join(\"\");\n}\nvar cards = HUES.map(function (h, i) {\n  var card = document.createElement(\"div\"); card.className = \"rl-card\"; card.style.background = \"linear-gradient(160deg, #15161b, #0c0d10)\"; card.style.zIndex = i;\n  var shot = document.createElement(\"div\"); shot.className = \"rl-shot\"; shot.innerHTML = screen(h); card.appendChild(shot);\n  var edge = document.createElement(\"div\"); edge.className = \"rl-edge\"; edge.style.borderRadius = radius + \"px\"; card.appendChild(edge);\n  frameEl.appendChild(card);\n  return { card: card, shot: shot };\n});\nvar total = (cards.length - 1) * stepF + revealF;\nfunction draw(frame) {\n  cards.forEach(function (c, i) {\n    var pr = interp(frame, [i * stepF, i * stepF + revealF], [0, 1], outCubic);\n    if (pr <= 0) { c.card.style.opacity = 0; return; }\n    var inset = (1 - pr) * 50;\n    c.card.style.opacity = 1;\n    c.card.style.clipPath = \"inset(\" + inset + \"% \" + inset + \"% round \" + radius + \"px)\";\n    c.shot.style.transform = \"scale(\" + lerp(1.08, 1, pr) + \")\";\n  });\n}\nfinish(drive(draw, Math.max(TOTAL, total)));\n\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
